amiento adecuado del cuerpo.\",30\r\n13784,CÉLULAS HEMATOPIÉTICAS,Células hematopoyéticas son células madre que se desarrollan en la médula ósea y son responsables de la producción de todas las células sanguíneas.,8\r\n4186,CAD,\"CAD, or Coronary Artery Disease, is a condition that can complicate diabetes management and requires specific dietary considerations. However, the term CAD is also used to refer to diabetic ketoacidosis, a serious complication of diabetes characterized by high levels of ketones in the blood due to insufficient insulin. This condition leads to metabolic acidosis and is a critical health concern for individuals with diabetes. It is important to differentiate between these two meanings of CAD, as one pertains to heart health and the other to a severe metabolic state resulting from diabetes.\",9\r\n2252,BICARBONATO,\"Bicarbonate, also known as bicarbonato, is a chemical compound that plays a crucial role in maintaining the pH balance in the body, with normal levels typically ranging between 22 and 29 mmol/l. It acts as a buffer, helping to regulate acidity and alkalinity in various physiological processes. Bicarbonate is particularly significant in medical contexts, as it is often measured in patients with diabetic ketoacidosis to assess their metabolic status and is used in treatments to correct acidosis. Additionally, it is recognized as an electrolyte that can be affected in patients experiencing secretory diarrhea, potentially leading to electrolyte imbalances.\n\nResearch has also explored the potential effects of bicarbonate on exercise performance and muscle function, indicating its broader relevance beyond just metabolic health. Overall, bicarbonate is an essential substance in both clinical and physiological settings, contributing to the body's homeostasis and being utilized in various medical treatments.\",5\r\n13785,DIARREA SECRETORA,La diarrea secretora es una condición que puede causar pérdidas importantes de electrolitos en pacien